#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176983 :tutorial/content "Consider the region enclosed by the curves $x=f(y)$ on the right, $x=g(y)$ on the left, and the horizontal lines $y=c$ and $y=d,$ as shown below. We assume that $f(y) \\geq g(y)$ for all $y \\in [c,d].$ \n\n![](images/9a/9a3970253f710223a77fe43f717df908fc20f27950744166ea7197897d64936d.png)\n\nTo find the volume of the solid generated when this region is rotated $2\\pi$ radians about the $x$-axis, we use the shell method as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{c}^{d}y([\\text{right}]-[\\text{left}])\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{c}^{d}y([f(y)]-[g(y)])\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "ee650309-6a00-514b-83cf-cc7028b14529" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5293 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
